    "html": "<section class=\"lens-view lens-dispatch-view\"><h3>network-line-graph-edge-vectors · 5×1×1 workgroups × 256×1×1 lanes = 1280 invocations</h3><svg class=\"lens-workgroups\" viewBox=\"0 0 640 24\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Workgroups\"><defs><pattern id=\"lens-gpu-network-network-line-graph-kernel-hatched\" patternUnits=\"userSpaceOnUse\" width=\"6\" height=\"6\" patternTransform=\"rotate(45)\"><line x1=\"0\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"0\" y2=\"6\" stroke=\"#595959\" stroke-width=\"1\"></line></pattern></defs><rect x=\"1\" y=\"1\" width=\"17\" height=\"17\" data-provenance=\"metadata\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#181818\" stroke-width=\"3\" data-state=\"selection\" data-action=\"bind\" data-axis=\"workgroup\" data-key=\"0\"></rect><rect x=\"21\" y=\"1\" width=\"17\" height=\"17\" data-provenance=\"metadata\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1\" data-action=\"bind\" data-axis=\"workgroup\" data-key=\"1\"></rect><rect x=\"41\" y=\"1\" width=\"17\" height=\"17\" data-provenance=\"metadata\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1\" data-action=\"bind\" data-axis=\"workgroup\" data-key=\"2\"></rect><rect x=\"61\" y=\"1\" width=\"17\" height=\"17\" data-provenance=\"metadata\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1\" data-action=\"bind\" data-axis=\"workgroup\" data-key=\"3\"></rect><rect x=\"81\" y=\"1\" width=\"17\" height=\"17\" data-provenance=\"metadata\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1\" data-action=\"bind\" data-axis=\"workgroup\" data-key=\"4\"></rect></svg><h4>Workgroup 0 (default)</h4><svg class=\"lens-lanes\" viewBox=\"0 0 1280 256\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Lanes in expanded workgroup\"><defs><pattern id=\"lens-gpu-network-network-line-graph-kernel-lanes-hatched\" patternUnits=\"userSpaceOnUse\" width=\"6\" height=\"6\" patternTransform=\"rotate(45)\"><line x1=\"0\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"0\" y2=\"6\" stroke=\"#595959\" stroke-width=\"1\"></line></pattern></defs><image width=\"1280\" height=\"256\" preserveAspectRatio=\"none\" image-rendering=\"pixelated\" data-provenance=\"metadata\" data-raster-width=\"32\" data-raster-height=\"8\" data-sampling=\"nearest\" href=\"data:image/png;base64,\"></image><g data-action=\"pick\" data-axis=\"lane\" data-key=\"0\"><text x=\"5\" y=\"21\" fill=\"currentColor\" data-provenance=\"metadata\">0</text></g><g data-action=\"pick\" data-axis=\"lane\" data-key=\"1\"><text x=\"45\" y=\"21\" fill=\"currentColor\" data-provenance=\"metadata\">1</text></g><g data-action=\"pick\" data-axis=\"lane\" data-key=\"2\"><text x=\"85\" y=\"21\" fill=\"currentColor\" data-provenance=\"metadata\">2</text></g><g data-action=\"pick\" data-axis=\"lane\" data-key=\"3\"><text x=\"125\" y=\"21\" fill=\"currentColor\" data-provenance=\"metadata\">3</text></g><g data-action=\"pick\" data-axis=\"lane\" data-key=\"4\"><text x=\"165\" y=\"21\" fill=\"currentColor\" data-provenance=\"metadata\">4</text></g><g data-action=\"pick\" data-axis=\"lane\" data-key=\"5\"><text x=\"205\" y=\"21\" fill=\"currentColor\" data-provenance=\"metadata\">5</text></g><g data-action=\"pick\" data-axis=\"lane\" data-key=\"6\"><text x=\"245\" y=\"21\" fill=\"currentColor\" data-provenance=\"metadata\">6</text></g><g data-action=\"pick\" data-axis=\"lane\" data-key=\"7\"><text x=\"285\" y=\"21\" fill=\"currentColor\" data-provenance=\"metadata\">7</text></g><g data-action=\"pick\" data-axis=\"lane\" data-key=\"8\"><text x=\"325\" y=\"21\" fill=\"currentColor\" data-provenance=\"metadata\">8</text></g><g data-action=\"pick\" data-axis=\"lane\" data-key=\"9\"><text x=\"365\" y=\"21\" fill=\"currentColor\" data-provenance=\"metadata\">9</text></g><g data-action=\"pick\" data-axis=\"lane\" data-key=\"10\"><text x=\"405\" y=\"21\" fill=\"currentColor\" data-provenance=\"metadata\">10</text></g><g data-action=\"pick\" data-axis=\"lane\" data-key=\"11\"><text x=\"445\" y=\"21\" fill=\"currentColor\" data-provenance=\"metadata\">11</text></g><g data-action=\"pick\" data-axis=\"lane\" data-key=\"12\"><text x=\"485\" y=\"21\" fill=\"currentColor\" data-provenance=\"metadata\">12</text></g><g data-action=\"pick\" data-axis=\"lane\" data-key=\"13\"><text x=\"525\" y=\"21\" fill=\"currentColor\" data-provenance=\"metadata\">13</text></g><g data-action=\"pick\" data-axis=\"lane\" data-key=\"14\"><text x=\"565\" y=\"21\" fill=\"currentColor\" data-provenance=\"metadata\">14</text></g></svg><p>256 lanes; first 15 and pinned lane labelled. Grey cells are idle or unavailable.</p><p>id probe not recorded; lane ids are computed from the dispatch shape · apple</p><figure class=\"lens-kernel-source\"><pre><code data-language=\"wgsl\"><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"1\">\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"2\">override INVOCATION_COUNT: u32;\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"3\">override WGSL_KERNEL_DISPATCH_X: u32;\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"4\">override WGSL_KERNEL_DISPATCH_Y: u32;\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"5\">const offsetsOffset: u32 = 0u;\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line lens-source-line--binding\" data-line=\"6\">@group(0) @binding(0) var&lt;storage, read&gt; offsets: array&lt;u32&gt;;\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"7\">const neighborsOffset: u32 = 0u;\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line lens-source-line--binding\" data-line=\"8\">@group(0) @binding(1) var&lt;storage, read&gt; neighbors: array&lt;u32&gt;;\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"9\">const nodePositionsOffset: u32 = 0u;\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line lens-source-line--binding\" data-line=\"10\">@group(0) @binding(2) var&lt;storage, read&gt; nodePositions: array&lt;f32&gt;;\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"11\">const edgeVectorsOffset: u32 = 0u;\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line lens-source-line--binding\" data-line=\"12\">@group(0) @binding(3) var&lt;storage, read_write&gt; edgeVectors: array&lt;f32&gt;;\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"13\">const NODE_COUNT: u32 = 1199u;\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"14\">const EDGE_COUNT: u32 = 2810u;\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"15\">\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"16\">\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"17\">fn geodesicAtan2(y: f32, x: f32) -&gt; f32 {\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"18\">  return select(atan2(y, x), sign(y) * 1.5707963267948966, x == 0.0);\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"19\">}\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"20\">\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"21\">const GEODESIC_PI: f32 = 3.14159265358979;\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"22\">// Component reconstruction avoids polar and long-path cancellation; these boundaries\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"23\">// retain the established short-path arithmetic and are covered by the PROJ regressions.\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"24\">const GEODESIC_DIRECT_COMPONENT_ANGLE: f32 = 0.25 * GEODESIC_PI;\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"25\">const GEODESIC_DIRECT_POLAR_LATITUDE: f32 = 80.0;\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"26\">const GEODESIC_DIRECT_POLAR_SINE: f32 = 0.984807753012208; // sin(80 degrees)\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"27\">const GEODESIC_DEGREES_TO_RADIANS: f32 = 0.0174532925199433;\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"28\">const GEODESIC_RADIANS_TO_DEGREES: f32 = 57.2957795130823;\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"29\">\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"30\">fn geodesicWrapLongitudeDelta(delta: f32) -&gt; f32 {\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"31\">  return delta - 360.0 * round(delta / 360.0);\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"32\">}\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"33\">\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"34\">// Subtract near the shared antimeridian before forming the small angular separation.\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"35\">// Wrapping (destination - source) afterward cannot recover bits lost by that large subtraction:\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"36\">// 179.341 -&gt; -179.877 loses about 1.6 meters on the OpenFlights sphere fixture.\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"37\">fn geodesicLongitudeDelta(source: f32, destination: f32) -&gt; f32 {\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"38\">  // WGSL permits floating-point reassociation: the two seam-relative subtractions below\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"39\">  // can become (destination - source) - 2 * halfTurn, restoring the cancellation.\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"40\">  // For opposite seam quadrants, every f32 endpoint is exactly a multiple of 2^-17\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"41\">  // degrees (the smallest ulp on [90, 180]). Scale by that power of two and wrap in\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"42\">  // i32: magnitudes stay below 2^26, with no quantization or integer overflow. Only\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"43\">  // the final, small difference is converted back to f32, so reassociation cannot\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"44\">  // reintroduce a large floating-point subtraction.\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"45\">  if (abs(source) &gt; 90.0 &amp;&amp; abs(source) &lt;= 180.0 &amp;&amp;\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"46\">      abs(destination) &gt; 90.0 &amp;&amp; abs(destination) &lt;= 180.0 &amp;&amp;\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"47\">      ((source &lt; 0.0) != (destination &lt; 0.0))) {\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"48\">    let sourceUnits = i32(source * 131072.0);\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"49\">    let destinationUnits = i32(destination * 131072.0);\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"50\">    let turnUnits = select(-47185920, 47185920, source &gt; 0.0);\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"51\">    return f32(destinationUnits - sourceUnits + turnUnits) * 0.00000762939453125;\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"52\">  }\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"53\">  let halfTurn = 180.0 * round((destination - source) / 360.0);\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"54\">  return (destination - halfTurn) - (source + halfTurn);\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"55\">}\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"56\">\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"57\">// cos(latitude) as sin(colatitude): 90 - |lat| is exact in f32, so the cosine keeps its relative\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"58\">// precision near the poles where cos(lat * pi / 180) would not.\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"59\">fn geodesicCosLatitude(latitudeDegrees: f32) -&gt; f32 {\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"60\">  return sin((90.0 - abs(latitudeDegrees)) * GEODESIC_DEGREES_TO_RADIANS);\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"61\">}\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"62\">\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"63\">fn geodesicUnitVector(lngLat: vec2&lt;f32&gt;) -&gt; vec3&lt;f32&gt; {\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"64\">  let lambda = lngLat.x * GEODESIC_DEGREES_TO_RADIANS;\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"65\">  let phi = lngLat.y * GEODESIC_DEGREES_TO_RADIANS;\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"66\">  let cosPhi = geodesicCosLatitude(lngLat.y);\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"67\">  return vec3&lt;f32&gt;(cosPhi * cos(lambda), cosPhi * sin(lambda), sin(phi));\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"68\">}\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"69\">\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"70\">fn geodesicFromUnitVector(vector: vec3&lt;f32&gt;) -&gt; vec2&lt;f32&gt; {\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"71\">  let horizontal = sqrt(vector.x * vector.x + vector.y * vector.y);\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"72\">  return vec2&lt;f32&gt;(\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"73\">    geodesicAtan2(vector.y, vector.x) * GEODESIC_RADIANS_TO_DEGREES,\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"74\">    geodesicAtan2(vector.z, horizontal) * GEODESIC_RADIANS_TO_DEGREES\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"75\">  );\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"76\">}\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"77\">\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"78\">fn geodesicHaversineTerm(a: vec2&lt;f32&gt;, b: vec2&lt;f32&gt;) -&gt; f32 {\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"79\">  let deltaPhi = (b.y - a.y) * GEODESIC_DEGREES_TO_RADIANS;\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"80\">  let deltaLambda = geodesicLongitudeDelta(a.x, b.x) * GEODESIC_DEGREES_TO_RADIANS;\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"81\">  let sinHalfPhi = sin(0.5 * deltaPhi);\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"82\">  let sinHalfLambda = sin(0.5 * deltaLambda);\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"83\">  let term = sinHalfPhi * sinHalfPhi +\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"84\">    geodesicCosLatitude(a.y) * geodesicCosLatitude(b.y) *\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"85\">    sinHalfLambda * sinHalfLambda;\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"86\">  return clamp(term, 0.0, 1.0);\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"87\">}\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"88\">\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"89\">// East, north and up components of b in the local frame at a. Near an antipode,\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"90\">// use the latitude sum and longitude supplement to avoid subtracting order-one terms.\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"91\">fn geodesicBearingComponents(origin: vec2&lt;f32&gt;, targetPosition: vec2&lt;f32&gt;) -&gt; vec3&lt;f32&gt; {\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"92\">  if (origin.y == targetPosition.y &amp;&amp; (geodesicLongitudeDelta(origin.x, targetPosition.x) == 0.0 || abs(origin.y) == 90.0)) {\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"93\">    return vec3&lt;f32&gt;(0.0, 0.0, 1.0);\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"94\">  }\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"95\">  let latitudeRadians = origin.y * GEODESIC_DEGREES_TO_RADIANS;\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"96\">  let targetLatitudeRadians = targetPosition.y * GEODESIC_DEGREES_TO_RADIANS;\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"97\">  let longitudeDeltaDegrees = geodesicLongitudeDelta(origin.x, targetPosition.x);\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"98\">  let longitudeDeltaRadians = longitudeDeltaDegrees * GEODESIC_DEGREES_TO_RADIANS;\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"99\">  let originCosine = geodesicCosLatitude(origin.y);\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"100\">  let targetCosine = geodesicCosLatitude(targetPosition.y);\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"101\">  let halfSineLongitude = sin(0.5 * longitudeDeltaRadians);\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"102\">  let halfVersine = 2.0 * halfSineLongitude * halfSineLongitude;\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"103\">  var east = targetCosine * sin(longitudeDeltaRadians);\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"104\">  var north = sin((targetPosition.y - origin.y) * GEODESIC_DEGREES_TO_RADIANS) +\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"105\">    sin(latitudeRadians) * targetCosine * halfVersine;\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"106\">  var longitudeCosine = 1.0 - halfVersine;\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"107\">  // A small longitude supplement does not imply a near antipode: two points at\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"108\">  // the same pole can have opposite longitudes. Their latitude sum is near 180\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"109\">  // degrees, where taking its sine loses the colatitude&#39;s relative precision.\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"110\">  if (abs(longitudeDeltaDegrees) &gt; 90.0 &amp;&amp; origin.y * targetPosition.y &lt;= 0.0) {\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"111\">    let supplement = (180.0 - abs(longitudeDeltaDegrees)) * GEODESIC_DEGREES_TO_RADIANS;\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"112\">    let halfSine = sin(0.5 * supplement);\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"113\">    east = targetCosine * sign(longitudeDeltaDegrees) * sin(supplement);\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"114\">    north = sin((origin.y + targetPosition.y) * GEODESIC_DEGREES_TO_RADIANS) -\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"115\">      2.0 * sin(latitudeRadians) * targetCosine * halfSine * halfSine;\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"116\">    longitudeCosine = 2.0 * halfSine * halfSine - 1.0;\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"117\">  }\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"118\">  let vertical = sin(latitudeRadians) * sin(targetLatitudeRadians) + originCosine * targetCosine * longitudeCosine;\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"119\">  return vec3&lt;f32&gt;(east, north, vertical);\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"120\">}\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"121\">\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"122\">fn geodesicCentralAngle(a: vec2&lt;f32&gt;, b: vec2&lt;f32&gt;) -&gt; f32 {\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"123\">  let components = geodesicBearingComponents(a, b);\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"124\">  return geodesicAtan2(sqrt(components.x * components.x + components.y * components.y), components.z);\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"125\">}\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"126\">\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"127\">fn geodesicInitialBearingDegrees(a: vec2&lt;f32&gt;, b: vec2&lt;f32&gt;) -&gt; f32 {\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"128\">  let components = geodesicBearingComponents(a, b);\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"129\">  return geodesicAtan2(components.x, components.y) * GEODESIC_RADIANS_TO_DEGREES;\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"130\">}\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"131\">\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"132\">fn geodesicDestination(origin: vec2&lt;f32&gt;, bearingDegrees: f32, angle: f32) -&gt; vec2&lt;f32&gt; {\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"133\">  if (angle == 0.0) { return origin; }\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"134\">  let phi1 = origin.y * GEODESIC_DEGREES_TO_RADIANS;\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"135\">  let theta = bearingDegrees * GEODESIC_DEGREES_TO_RADIANS;\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"136\">  let sinPhi1 = sin(phi1);\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"137\">  let cosPhi1 = geodesicCosLatitude(origin.y);\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"138\">  let sinHalfAngle = sin(0.5 * angle);\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"139\">  // sin(phi2) - sin(phi1), from the half-angle form so short moves keep their precision.\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"140\">  let sinDelta = -2.0 * sinPhi1 * sinHalfAngle * sinHalfAngle + cosPhi1 * sin(angle) * cos(theta);\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"141\">  let sinPhi2 = clamp(sinPhi1 + sinDelta, -1.0, 1.0);\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"142\">  // The half-angle change below preserves ordinary short moves. At a polar\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"143\">  // origin or arrival (within 10 degrees of a pole), use components instead of asin.\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"144\">  // Long paths also cancel in sinPhi1 + sinDelta and in the longitude denominator.\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"145\">  // Preserve the established half-angle change only for short ordinary paths.\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"146\">  if (abs(angle) &gt;= GEODESIC_DIRECT_COMPONENT_ANGLE || abs(origin.y) &gt;= GEODESIC_DIRECT_POLAR_LATITUDE || abs(sinPhi2) &gt;= GEODESIC_DIRECT_POLAR_SINE) {\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"147\">    let east = sin(theta) * sin(angle);\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"148\">    let north = cosPhi1 * cos(angle) - sinPhi1 * sin(angle) * cos(theta);\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"149\">    let vertical = sinPhi1 * cos(angle) + cosPhi1 * sin(angle) * cos(theta);\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"150\">    let horizontal = sqrt(east * east + north * north);\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"151\">    // Above 45 degrees, recover the latitude from the colatitude: atan2(vertical, horizontal)\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"152\">    // returns a value near pi/2 whose absolute error (about a meter in f32) would swamp short\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"153\">    // polar moves, while the colatitude keeps the horizontal component&#39;s relative precision.\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"154\">    var latitudeDegrees = geodesicAtan2(vertical, horizontal) * GEODESIC_RADIANS_TO_DEGREES;\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"155\">    if (abs(vertical) &gt; horizontal) {\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"156\">      latitudeDegrees = sign(vertical) * (90.0 - geodesicAtan2(horizontal, abs(vertical)) * GEODESIC_RADIANS_TO_DEGREES);\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"157\">    }\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"158\">    // A short move from a polar origin still takes the half-angle latitude change, added in\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"159\">    // degrees: converting a polar latitude to f32 radians alone costs about 0.4 m, which the\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"160\">    // component form inherits. The midpoint cosine guard hands the last 0.06 degrees to the\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"161\">    // colatitude.\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"162\">    if (abs(angle) &lt; GEODESIC_DIRECT_COMPONENT_ANGLE) {\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"163\">      let midpointCosine = cos(0.5 * (phi1 + asin(sinPhi2)));\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"164\">      if (abs(midpointCosine) &gt; 1e-3) {\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"165\">        latitudeDegrees = origin.y + 2.0 * asin(clamp(sinDelta / (2.0 * midpointCosine), -1.0, 1.0)) * GEODESIC_RADIANS_TO_DEGREES;\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"166\">      }\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"167\">    }\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"168\">    return vec2&lt;f32&gt;(\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"169\">      origin.x + geodesicAtan2(east, north) * GEODESIC_RADIANS_TO_DEGREES,\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"170\">      latitudeDegrees\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"171\">    );\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"172\">  }\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"173\">  let roughPhi2 = asin(sinPhi2);\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"174\">  // sin(phi2) - sin(phi1) = 2 cos((phi1 + phi2) / 2) sin((phi2 - phi1) / 2); the midpoint cosine\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"175\">  // is insensitive to the rough phi2, so the latitude change is recovered to relative precision.\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"176\">  let midpointCosine = cos(0.5 * (phi1 + roughPhi2));\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"177\">  var deltaPhi = roughPhi2 - phi1;\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"178\">  if (abs(midpointCosine) &gt; 1e-3) {\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"179\">    deltaPhi = 2.0 * asin(clamp(sinDelta / (2.0 * midpointCosine), -1.0, 1.0));\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"180\">  }\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"181\">  let deltaLambda = geodesicAtan2(\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"182\">    sin(theta) * sin(angle) * cosPhi1,\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"183\">    cos(angle) - sinPhi1 * sinPhi2\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"184\">  );\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"185\">  return vec2&lt;f32&gt;(\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"186\">    origin.x + deltaLambda * GEODESIC_RADIANS_TO_DEGREES,\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"187\">    origin.y + deltaPhi * GEODESIC_RADIANS_TO_DEGREES\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"188\">  );\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"189\">}\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"190\">\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"191\">fn geodesicInterpolate(a: vec2&lt;f32&gt;, b: vec2&lt;f32&gt;, angle: f32, fraction: f32) -&gt; vec2&lt;f32&gt; {\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"192\">  // Endpoints are known even when the interior path is nonunique or ill-conditioned.\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"193\">  if (fraction == 0.0) { return a; }\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"194\">  if (fraction == 1.0) {\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"195\">    if (abs(b.x - a.x) &lt;= 180.0) { return b; }\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"196\">    return vec2&lt;f32&gt;(a.x + geodesicLongitudeDelta(a.x, b.x), b.y);\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"197\">  }\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"198\">  if (GEODESIC_PI - angle &lt; 1e-6) {\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"199\">    return vec2&lt;f32&gt;(bitcast&lt;f32&gt;(0x7fc00000u | (bitcast&lt;u32&gt;(a.x) &amp; 0u)));\n</span><span class=\"lens-source-line\" data-line=\"200\">  }\n</span></code></pre><p>119 source lines omitted</p><table><thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Resource</th><th>Access</th><th>Element type</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>offsets<span class=\"lens-provenance lens-provenance--metadata\" title=\"Static metadata, not an execution measurement.\">metadata</span></td><td data-action=\"bind\" data-axis=\"buffer\" data-key=\"gpu-network.network-line-graph-offsets\">gpu-network.network-line-graph-offsets</td><td>read</td><td>u32</td></tr><tr><td>neighbors<span class=\"lens-provenance lens-provenance--metadata\" title=\"Static metadata, not an execution measurement.\">metadata</span></td><td data-action=\"bind\" data-axis=\"buffer\" data-key=\"gpu-network.network-line-graph-neighbors\">gpu-network.network-line-graph-neighbors</td><td>read</td><td>u32</td></tr><tr><td>nodeP